WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:07.680
Invariably I would see buses going down into South Baton Rouge.

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:18.860
And on those buses were maids and cooks and so forth who had come from the white area of Goodwood and other areas.

3
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.640
The maids, who had cooked for whites, were not able to sit down.

4
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.700
And of course, there were only blacks down there,

5
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:36.220
and the whites who were living in South Baton Rouge were those whites who had businesses such as grocery stores and what have you,

6
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.640
and were making a living off of blacks.

7
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:47.920
I thought it was terrible that they could work all day for white folks and couldn’t sit down on the bus . . .

8
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.040
The blacks going down into South Baton Rouge were forced to stand up over empty seats.

9
00:00:54.040 --> 00:01:01.520
They could put their bags, their bundles in the seat, but they couldn’t put their bodies.

10
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.000
And of course I thought that was ridiculous.

11
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:13.880
And I was much younger then and I was more daring and I thought that we had to do something about that.

12
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.100
And of course we did.
